  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Guests and clients pay for consistent taste, safe food and reliable service. They judge you by quality, timing and how you handle problems.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is knowing the cost of every dish and the price that keeps a healthy margin.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and restaurant, catering and food business: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools help plan menus, forecast stock and handle bookings. Routine ordering and planning shrink.
  </p>
  <p>
    Taste, hygiene, leadership and guest care hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to plan and cost; later, own quality and customers.
  </p>

